===============================================================================
Stacked Bar Chart Visualization of Study Participants and Authors by Gender/Sex
===============================================================================

This Python script generates a stacked bar chart that illustrates the percentage
distribution of study participants and authors according to gender/sex categories.
It provides a detailed visualization for scientific reporting, allowing for
comparisons between participant sex and author sex (first and last authors).

Features:
- Converts absolute counts to percentages for clear visualization.
- Dynamically adjusts bar colors with tone and transparency parameters.
- Displays percentage labels inside each bar with automatic text color adjustment.
- Configures a horizontal legend displayed below the chart in right-to-left order.
- Formats the Y-axis to include the percent symbol.
- Saves the figure in JPEG, TIFF, and EPS formats via a file dialog.

